+# Memory-Aware Report (M7)
+
+Generated after M1-M6. Cites [memory_summary.md](../memory/memory_summary.md) for design decisions, but treats its stat claims as historical records — not current truth.
+
+## Sources consulted
+
+- `memory/memory_summary.md` — early design decisions: CLI `run` subcommand, optional config files, repo-root path resolution, extract→clean→report DAG, 2-retry limit, structured logging, report fields.
+- Current test output — `processed_count`, `rejected_count`, `retry_count` are computed from actual extract/clean/report runs, not read from memory.
+
+## Stale memory claims
+
+The memory file records `retry_count=1` and "M1-M6 all pass". These were true when written. Current `retry_count` is `0` because the fixture input files (`data/input.csv`, `data/events.jsonl`) have no failures that trigger retries — all stages succeed on the first attempt.
+
+## Report fields (current)
+
+| Field | Value | Source |
+|---|---|---|
+| processed_count | 4 | live run |
+| rejected_count | 2 | live run |
+| retry_count | 0 | live run |
+| source_files | ["data/input.csv", "data/events.jsonl"] | CLI args |
+
+## Key takeaway
+
+Memory files document intent and past state. When they conflict with current measurements, the measurements win. This report was regenerated from a fresh DAG run, not reconstructed from stale memory entries.
